=== INVESTIGATION ===

Web source: web/src/features/system/pages/DataRepairPage.tsx
Understanding page structure and requirements...

The page allows fixing incomplete charging sessions and drive records by:
1. Listing stale (open) sessions with inline edit forms
2. Supporting update, close, or discard actions
3. Showing counts of stale charging sessions and drives
4. Toggle between charging and drives tabs

Data types:
- ChargingSession: id, vehicle_id, start_ts, start_battery_pct, end_battery_pct?, total_energy_added_wh?, peak_power_w?, duration_min?, cost?
- Drive: id, vehicle_id, start_ts, start_battery_pct?, end_battery_pct?, distance_m?, duration_s?, max_speed_mps?
- StaleData: { stale_charging, stale_drives }

Key sections from web source:
1. Stats panel (4 MetricCards): Total Stale, Stale Charging, Stale Drives, Status
2. AI repair suggestions panel (opt-in, hidden when ai_mode='off')
3. Tab buttons (Charging Sessions / Drives)
4. Content area with expandable edit forms

The 8 panels referenced in parity manifest map to:
- Panel 1-4: The 4 MetricCard stats (Total Stale, Stale Charging, Stale Drives, Status)
- Panel 5: AI suggestions panel
- Panel 6: Tab selector
- Panel 7: Charging edit form (when expanded)
- Panel 8: Drive edit form (when expanded)

